questions.explanation:
$$f(x) = \left\{ {\matrix{
   { - 55x,} &amp; {if\,x &lt;  - 5}  \cr 
   {2{x^3} - 3{x^2} - 120x,} &amp; {if\, - 5 \le x \le 4}  \cr 
   {2{x^3} - 3{x^2} - 36x - 336,} &amp; {if\,x &gt; 4,}  \cr 

 } } \right.$$


Now, $$f'(x) = \left\{ {\matrix{
   { - 55} &amp; ; &amp; {x &lt;  - 5}  \cr 
   {6({x^2} - x - 20)} &amp; ; &amp; { - 5 &lt; x &lt; 4}  \cr 
   {6({x^2} - x - 6)} &amp; ; &amp; {x &gt; 4}  \cr 

 } } \right.$$

$$f'(x) = \left\{ {\matrix{
   { - 55} &amp; ; &amp; {x &lt;  - 5}  \cr 
   {6(x - 5)(x + 4)} &amp; ; &amp; { - 5 &lt; x &lt; 4}  \cr 
   {6(x - 3)(x + 2)} &amp; ; &amp; {x &gt; 4}  \cr 

 } } \right.$$

Hence, f(x) is monotonically increasing in interval $$( - 5, - 4) \cup (4,\infty )$$
